{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Gather yourselves, yes, gather</b> — the meaning is: argue and reprove. And R. Moses said: gather and assemble, from the root of מקושש קש (gathering stubble), which is to collect straw. And others said: like the Aramaic translation of זקנתי ושבתי (I have grown old and turned back)." "<b>Not desired</b> — it is not loved and desirable to the nations, from the root of נכספה וגם כלתה (it has longed and also pined away)."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:18.644605547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}